Chapter: RiderSpec
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils
  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Safari chapter Geom
  cites Safari chapter Pose
  cites Safari chapter Bike
  cites Safari chapter VehicleLimits
  cites Safari chapter World
  cites Safari chapter Arc
  cites Safari chapter LeanSearch
  cites Safari chapter Throttle
  cites Safari chapter Gaze
  cites Safari chapter Rider
  cites Judge chapter Grade

 Rider: one frame. Decide the controls, run the physics, then resolve the road
 graph by POSITION.

 THE THROTTLE ANSWERS THE BIKE HE IS ABOUT TO BE. `decide` picks the lean first
 and then asks for the acceleration of the LEANED state, not the current one --
 so a rider about to bank hard is already told to stop accelerating. Reading the
 current tilt instead would let him power into the lean for one frame, every
 frame, and look almost right.

 THE SEAM CHANGES THE FRAME AND NOT THE BEARING. Crossing into the next segment
 re-expresses the same physical point in the next segment's coordinates: the
 frame-relative yaw rotates by the turn while the ABSOLUTE heading does not move
 at all. That pair is the assertion -- a chapter turning both would have him
 drifting off north by the sum of the route's corners, which nothing on screen
 shows directly.

 SPEED AND LEAN CARRY ACROSS AND THE GAZE DOES NOT: his eyes go back on the road
 at a seam, but the FOCUS carries, so the lens keeps easing open instead of
 snapping. Three fields, three different rules, all graded.

 THE FINISH SNAP EXISTS BECAUSE OF A ZENO STALL, which the chapter says outright.
 The kinematic brake would leave him a hair short of the line forever -- stopped
 and never finished -- so inside the braking zone a crawl counts as arrival. Both
 arms are graded: over the line, and short of it but slow.

 We say:

Section: Deciding

  segs : List Segment
  segs = [segment-at 0, segment-at 1, segment-at 2]

  seg : Segment
  seg = segment-at 0

  rider : Real, Real, Real, Real -> RiderState
  rider (along) (across) (v) (tilt) =
    RiderState { segment = 0, along = along, across = across, yaw = 0.0, v = v,
                 tilt = tilt, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0 }

 The lean step takes him from where he is to what the search wants, so it is
 bounded by the search's own bracket.

  step-got : List Boolean
  step-got =
    let d = decide (rider 0.0 0.0 v-base 0.0) seg
    in let held = decide (rider 0.0 0.0 v-base 0.5) seg
    in [ real-abs d.tilt-step <= max-tilt-correction,
         real-abs held.tilt-step <= max-tilt-correction,
         d.accel <= a-accel + 0.000001 ]

  step-want : List Boolean
  step-want = [True, True, True]

 THE ACCELERATION IS THE LEANED BIKE'S. A rider upright but about to bank past
 the hold angle is told to stop accelerating this frame, which he would not be if
 the throttle read his current tilt.

  leaned-got : List Boolean
  leaned-got =
    let d = decide (rider 0.0 0.0 v-base 0.0) seg
    in let same = get-forward-accel-decel (with-tilt (rider 0.0 0.0 v-base 0.0) (0.0 + d.tilt-step)) seg
    in [d.accel ~0 same]

  leaned-want : List Boolean
  leaned-want = [True]

Section: Crossing A Seam

 The same physical point in the next segment's frame. Speed and lean carry
 untouched; the eyes go back on the road; the focus carries.

  at-seam : RiderState
  at-seam =
    RiderState { segment = 0, along = 499.0, across = 0.5, yaw = 0.1, v = 1.25,
                 tilt = 0.05, heading = 0.7, gaze-yaw = 0.3, focus = 0.4 }

  crossed : RiderState
  crossed = rider-state-for-next-segment at-seam segs

  carry-got : List Real
  carry-got = [crossed.v, crossed.tilt, crossed.focus, crossed.gaze-yaw]

  carry-want : List Real
  carry-want = [1.25, 0.05, 0.4, 0.0]

 THE HEADING DOES NOT MOVE AND THE YAW DOES. The crossing changes the frame, not
 the bearing, so the absolute heading is exactly what it was and the
 frame-relative yaw has turned by the segment's exit angle.

  turn-got : List Real
  turn-got =
    [ crossed.heading - 0.7,
      crossed.yaw - (0.1 - seg.exit-angle) ]

  turn-want : List Real
  turn-want = [0.0, 0.0]

  index-got : List Integer
  index-got = [crossed.segment, seg.exit-to]

  index-want : List Integer
  index-want = [1, 1]

 A rider nowhere near the seam re-expresses to a point far outside the next
 segment's lane, which is exactly how `resolve-cross` decides not to commit.

  early-got : List Boolean
  early-got =
    let far = rider-state-for-next-segment (rider 100.0 0.0 v-base 0.0) segs
    in [real-abs far.across >= (segment-at 1).width / 2.0]

  early-want : List Boolean
  early-want = [True]

Section: Resolving By Position

 He commits the moment his real point is inside the next segment, and not before.

  resolve-got : List Integer
  resolve-got =
    [ (resolve-cross (rider 100.0 0.0 v-base 0.0) seg segs).segment,
      (resolve-cross (rider 499.0 0.0 v-base 0.0) seg segs).segment ]

  resolve-want : List Integer
  resolve-want = [0, 1]

Section: The Finish

 The terminus has no segment to lead out, so he is clamped and stopped -- over the
 line, or short of it and crawling.

  last-seg : Segment
  last-seg = segment-at 18

  ended : Real, Real -> RiderState
  ended (along) (v) =
    finish-clamp (RiderState { segment = 0, along = along, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = v,
                               tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0 }) last-seg

  finish-got : List Real
  finish-got =
    [ (ended 300.0 0.5).along, (ended 300.0 0.5).v,
      (ended 310.0 0.5).along, (ended 310.0 0.5).v,
      (ended 290.0 0.05).along, (ended 290.0 0.05).v,
      (ended 290.0 0.5).along, (ended 290.0 0.5).v,
      (ended 100.0 0.05).along, (ended 100.0 0.05).v ]

  finish-want : List Real
  finish-want = [300.0, 0.0, 300.0, 0.0, 300.0, 0.0, 290.0, 0.5, 100.0, 0.05]

 A CRAWL ONLY COUNTS INSIDE THE ZONE. At a hundred metres out the same crawl is
 just a slow rider, which is the pair above that keeps the Zeno fix from
 stopping him anywhere on the course.

  done-got : List Boolean
  done-got =
    let at-end = RiderState { segment = 0, along = 300.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = 0.0,
                              tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0 }
    in let short = RiderState { segment = 0, along = 299.0, across = 0.0, yaw = 0.0, v = 0.0,
                                tilt = 0.0, heading = 0.0, gaze-yaw = 0.0, focus = 0.0 }
    in [ is-finished at-end [segment-at 18], is-finished short [segment-at 18],
         last-seg.terminates, is-finished (rider 499.0 0.0 v-base 0.0) segs ]

  done-want : List Boolean
  done-want = [True, False, True, False]

Section: One Whole Frame

 The controls, the physics and the resolve, together: he moves forward, he is
 still on the road, and nothing has gone backwards.

  next : RiderState
  next = get-next-rider-state (rider 0.0 0.0 v-base 0.0) segs

  frame-got : List Boolean
  frame-got =
    [ next.along > 0.0,
      next.v > 0.0,
      next.segment == 0,
      real-abs next.across < seg.width / 2.0,
      next.v <= v-max ]

  frame-want : List Boolean
  frame-want = [True, True, True, True, True]

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "rd-step  " step-got step-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "rd-leaned" leaned-got leaned-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "rd-carry " carry-got carry-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "rd-turn  " turn-got turn-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "rd-index " index-got index-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "rd-early " early-got early-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-ints  "rd-resolv" resolve-got resolve-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-reals "rd-finish" finish-got finish-want 0.0)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "rd-done  " done-got done-want)
    print-line-uni (grade-bools "rd-frame " frame-got frame-want)
  end
